WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
Tha sinn deiseil.

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
Oh aye, ok.

00:01.000 --> 00:04.000
Cuin agus carson a dh’fhàg sibh Astràilia?

00:04.000 --> 00:07.000
Uill, dh’fhàg mi thaobh cha robh còir agam a bhith ann, a’ chiad rud.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.000
Agus tàilleabh gun robh mi gu math involved

00:10.000 --> 00:13.000
leis a’ union, bha mi car… fhuair mi an toiseach air,

00:13.000 --> 00:16.000
fhuair mi a-staigh air a’… Chommunist Party.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.000
So an uairsin, bha mi taghta, cha tèideadh sgath ceàrr,

00:19.000 --> 00:22.000
an fheadhainn eile, bha waterfront làn dhiubh.

00:22.000 --> 00:25.000
Ach bha mi ro bhragail, bhithinnsa a’ dol

00:25.000 --> 00:29.000
chun na cùirtean a’ sabaid son na… fhios agad,

00:29.000 --> 00:31.000
son a’ Phartaidh ’s a h-uile sgath eile.

00:31.000 --> 00:33.000
So bha iad uabhasach laghach an uairsin, 

00:33.000 --> 00:35.000
bha a h-uile duine co-ordinating.

00:35.000 --> 00:38.000
Agus coltach gun tàinig fear dhe na poileasman, 

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
chaidh iad chun an union executive is thuirt iad:

00:42.000 --> 00:44.000
“’S fheàrr dha do– am balach a tha siud 

00:44.000 --> 00:46.000
a bheul a dhùinteadh, neo tha sinn a’ dol a chur air ais–

00:46.000 --> 00:48.000
a’ dol a thilleadh air ais, chionn chan eil còir aige–”

00:48.000 --> 00:50.000
Fhuair iad a-mach nach robh mi supposed a bhith siud idir.

00:50.000 --> 00:55.000
Nuair a chuala mise sin – dh’fhalbh mise, a bhalaich, às.

00:55.000 --> 00:58.000
Siud agad nuair a dh’fhalbh mi a New Zealand, nuair a dh’fhàg mi sin.

00:58.000 --> 01:00.000
B’ fheudar dhomh sin fhàg– so thug, an Welshman,

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
thug e staigh a New Zealand mi.

01:02.000 --> 01:04.000
A’ chiad job a bh’ againn, tha cuimhn’ am gu bràth,

01:04.000 --> 01:08.000
’s e lìonadh railway track de dh’iarann, scrap-iron,

01:08.000 --> 01:11.000
ga lìonadh, ga shadail, dh’obraicheadh pìosan mòra is na–

01:11.000 --> 01:14.000
oh, a Mhuire, bha dùil am gun robh mi dol a dhèanamh fortan

01:14.000 --> 01:15.000
ann an aon latha.

01:15.000 --> 01:19.000
Ach an rud a bha iad a’ dèanamh, a h-uile duine a bha ag obair,

01:19.000 --> 01:22.000
a thaobh cheud duin’, chuireadh iad ann a h-òrdain e

01:22.000 --> 01:24.000
is dh’innseadh iad dè chaidh a thogail an latha ud,

01:24.000 --> 01:27.000
agus bheireadh iad equals dhan a h-uile duine.

01:27.000 --> 01:30.000
Oh uill, an diabhal mise, bha an fhearg ormsa an uairsin.

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
Thuirt mi, agus bha an fhearg airsan cuideachd.

01:33.000 --> 01:35.000
Is thuirt mi: “Tillidh sinn air ais,

01:35.000 --> 01:37.000
agus chan eil sinn a’ dol a dhèanamh sgath airson…

01:37.000 --> 01:39.000
gus am faigh iad greim oirnn.”

01:39.000 --> 01:41.000
So, tha mi a’ smaoineachadh gun do thog mi dà latha eile,

01:41.000 --> 01:44.000
glè bheag an coimeas ri na dh’fhalbh air an trèana a bha sin.

01:44.000 --> 01:46.000
Ach fhuair mi an aon airgead a fhuair a h-uile duin’ eile.

01:46.000 --> 01:51.000
An uairsin dh’fhàg mi sin, ’s an uair a fhuair mi a-staigh a… 

01:51.000 --> 01:54.000
actually, chaidh sinn gu muir an uairsin ann an New Zealand.

01:54.000 --> 01:55.000
Chaidh mi air na bàtaichean is… 

01:55.000 --> 01:58.000
is tha cuimhn’ am an uairsin, bha mi, plan–

01:58.000 --> 01:59.000
a’ feuchainn ri faighinn air a’ waterfront,

01:59.000 --> 02:01.000
bha e uabhasach doirbh faighinn air a’ waterfront, 

02:01.000 --> 02:04.000
ach ’s e an job a b’ fheàrr a bh’ ann an New Zealand, sa waterfront.

02:04.000 --> 02:08.000
So tha cuimhn’ am gu bràth, dh’aoin mi bàta ’s e,

02:08.000 --> 02:12.000
b’ àbhaist dha Lieutenant General, ’s ann leis a bha an yacht a bha seo,

02:12.000 --> 02:16.000
chonverted airson tarraing orainsearan agus bananas 

02:16.000 --> 02:19.000
à Samoa sìos gu New Zealand.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.000
Agus bhiodh sinn a’ toirt suas biadh is rudan dhaibhsan,

02:22.000 --> 02:25.000
soft drinks, a h-uile sgath riamh, delivered.

02:25.000 --> 02:29.000
So dh’aoin mi am bàta sin, chaidh mi sìos gu Wellington

02:29.000 --> 02:31.000
leis a’ charago, agus thuirt mi ris,

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
cousin a bh’ agam ann an Auckland. 

02:33.000 --> 02:36.000
Thuirt mi, cha robh dad ri cousin, fhios agad,

02:36.000 --> 02:38.000
nuair a tha thu a’ bruidhinn Gàidhlig tha thu daonnan [...].

02:38.000 --> 02:40.000
Thuirt mi ris:

02:40.000 --> 02:43.000
“Ma gheibh thusa litir mu dheidhinn, ma chì thu litir bhuam,

02:43.000 --> 02:47.000
on waterfront, leugh– fosgail i,

02:47.000 --> 02:49.000
agus inns dhomh dè th’ innte. An rud a nì mi,”

02:49.000 --> 02:52.000
bho chionn cha robh phones an uairsin idir ann, ars mise dìreach, 

02:52.000 --> 02:56.000
“fòn neo telegram thugam, agus can gu bheil mo mhàthair,

02:56.000 --> 02:58.000
gu bheil i bochd, gun do ghabh i sròc,

02:58.000 --> 03:00.000
agus gum feum mi a dhol air ais a…  Auckland.”

03:00.000 --> 03:02.000
So, bha am bàta dìreach, cha mhòr, a’ falbh,

03:02.000 --> 03:05.000
air m’ onair a Dhia, agus cha tàinig an telegram neo sgath.

03:05.000 --> 03:07.000
Uill ghabh mi an, diabhal mise, bha agam ri dhol suas

03:07.000 --> 03:10.000
a Samoa a-nise. An ath rud, a laochain,

03:10.000 --> 03:13.000
a-nuas an quay, am postman, an deliveryman,

03:13.000 --> 03:15.000
bhiodh bicycle aca an uairsin,

03:15.000 --> 03:17.000
sìos a bhalaich leis a’ cheap is fallas air.

03:17.000 --> 03:21.000
Suas, ‘Captain!’ Suas an staidhre, bha e air am microphone:

03:21.000 --> 03:26.000
“Mr MacNeil, could you come up on the… up on the bridge?”

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
Chaidh mi suas, bha mi:

03:28.000 --> 03:29.000
“Oh, tha mi ’n dòchas nach eil sgath ceàrr.”

03:29.000 --> 03:31.000
Bha fios ’am fhìn dè bh’ anns an litir.

03:31.000 --> 03:34.000
“Oh,” he says, “where’s your mother?” I said: “She’s in Auckland.”

03:35.000 --> 03:37.000
“Oh, I’ve got bad news for you.”

03:37.000 --> 03:39.000
“How bad?”

03:39.000 --> 03:41.000
Ars esan: “She had a stroke.”

03:41.000 --> 03:44.000
“Oh, I’ve got to go, I can’t stay here.”

03:44.000 --> 03:48.000
Dh’fhalbh mi, a laochain, ’s fhuair mi air a’ phleana

03:48.000 --> 03:50.000
a dh’Auckland an oidhche sin.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.000
Thog an agent mi gus cuir suas chun an airport mi

03:52.000 --> 03:55.000
and off I was. Chaidh mi suas gu Auckland.

03:55.000 --> 03:58.000
Bha, oh, nuair a smaointicheas tu. Chaidh mi suas an-sin is…

03:58.000 --> 04:02.000
sin an aon, sin agad an weekend a bha mi twenty-one exactly,

04:02.000 --> 04:04.000
sin an aois a bha mi an uairsin, twenty-one.

04:04.000 --> 04:08.000
So cheannaich mi botal de Drambuie agus botal uisge-bheatha,

04:08.000 --> 04:11.000
agus thug mi suas iad gu mo chousin,

04:11.000 --> 04:13.000
agus dh’òl sinn cha mhòr fad na h-oidhche le na nàbaidhean

04:13.000 --> 04:15.000
’s a h-uile duine, thàinig iad mun cuairt,

04:15.000 --> 04:17.000
chionn bha iad daonnan airson èisteachd ri na naidheachdan,

04:17.000 --> 04:18.000
fhios agad, dè bha mi a’ dèanamh.

04:18.000 --> 04:22.000
So there you are, so. Sin mar a land mi an-sin an toiseach.

04:22.000 --> 04:24.000
Agus, a-rithist, cha do dh’fhuirich mi fada sa…

04:24.000 --> 04:27.000
air a’ waterfront. Dh’fhàg mi sin nam [XX]

04:27.000 --> 04:30.000
’s ghabh mi [XX] sìos dha na dùthaichean.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.000
Agus sin nuair a thachair mi, tha cuimhn’ am gu bràth,

04:32.000 --> 04:34.000
thachair mi ri dà Leòdhasach.

04:34.000 --> 04:36.000
Bha iad ag obair air… ann am Merry Merry, 

04:36.000 --> 04:39.000
stèisean mhòr a bh’ ann, hydro station.

04:39.000 --> 04:43.000
Agus bhiodh iad an uairsin, bha mise an Toronto, uh…

04:44.000 --> 04:50.000
an Auckland, air a’ waterfront. Agus bha apartment agam,

04:50.000 --> 04:52.000
so bhiodh weekend aca, thigeadh iad a choimhead ormsa

04:52.000 --> 04:55.000
’s a dhà neo trì son dhà neo trì botail is carry-on againn,

04:55.000 --> 05:02.000
the usual. Agus an uairsin… dh’eug m’ uncail,

05:02.000 --> 05:05.000
Am Patch a bh’ air. Dh’eug e shìos ann an Wellington,

05:05.000 --> 05:07.000
so chaidh mi sìos chun an tiodhlacadh aige.

05:07.000 --> 05:10.000
Agus an taigh anns an robh– am biodh iad a’ dol a choimhead orra,

05:10.000 --> 05:12.000
’s i tè Bharrach eile, thuirt i:

05:12.000 --> 05:15.000
“Seall thusa am feadan, ’s thoirt leat, ’s ann le d’ uncail a tha e.”

05:15.000 --> 05:18.000
Bha feadan aige is… “Oh it’s– bheir mi leam e.”

05:18.000 --> 05:21.000
So, thug mi suas dhan an apartment an Auckland e,

05:21.000 --> 05:24.000
agus aon weekend, thàinig mi dhachaigh,

05:24.000 --> 05:27.000
bha dà Leòdhasach a-staigh romham, agus chaidh mi dhan frids.

05:27.000 --> 05:32.000
Agus siud agad cearc agus am feadan suas an tòn aice. [laughs]

05:34.000 --> 05:36.000
Oh, nuair a smaointicheas thusa an carry-on a bh’ againne.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.000
Oh! So dh’ fhuirich mi sin, an uairsin chaidh mi,

05:41.000 --> 05:42.000
oh rinn mi a h-uile sgath dheth,

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
chaidh mi sìos chun an South Island.

05:44.000 --> 05:46.000
Bha mi ag obair actually, aon trup,

05:46.000 --> 05:48.000
fhios agad na casings son na sausages?

05:48.000 --> 05:50.000
Bha mi ag obair even as a… ann a shin,

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
chionn chaill mi m’ airgead, b’ fheudar dhomh job fhaighinn

05:52.000 --> 05:54.000
an-sin son seachdain neo ceala-deug.

05:54.000 --> 05:58.000
Bha obraichean anns a h-uile àite an-sin. Chòrd New Zealand rium.

05:58.000 --> 06:01.000
Agus an uairsin, of course, thàinig am [XX] 

06:01.000 --> 06:04.000
Barrach a bha seo, thuirt e:

06:04.000 --> 06:07.000
“Seo. Tha job agam air a’ bhàta dhut ma tha thu ga iarraidh.”

06:07.000 --> 06:09.000
So sin mar a land mi, fhuair mi cho fad ri…

06:09.000 --> 06:11.000
’s e Phanama agus thuirt mi:

06:11.000 --> 06:14.000
“Oh Dhia, chan eil toil agamsa a dhol nas fhaide na seo.”

06:14.000 --> 06:18.000
So leum mi am bàta ann am Panama, ach bha riots ann.

06:18.000 --> 06:21.000
Uill mun tàinig am bàta ron an [lot/?],

06:21.000 --> 06:23.000
chaidh mise air bòrd a-rithist, cha robh fhios aig an sgiobair

06:23.000 --> 06:25.000
gun do leum mi. [laughs]

06:25.000 --> 06:29.000
Roimhe sin, nuair– cho fad ’s a bha mi ann an New Zealand,

06:29.000 --> 06:31.000
air am bàta a chur suas gu Samoa,

06:31.000 --> 06:33.000
thòisich mi air reic transistor radios.

06:33.000 --> 06:35.000
Feadhainn bheaga, chionn, cha b’ urrainn dhut an ceannach

06:35.000 --> 06:37.000
ann an New Zealand idir, a thaobh bha,

06:37.000 --> 06:40.000
’s e socialist government a bh’ ann, agus cha robh luxury–

06:40.000 --> 06:45.000
no luxuries, a h-uile sgath riamh, hardcore… industry, chan…

06:46.000 --> 06:48.000
cha b’ urrainn dhut rèidio neo sgath a cheannach.

06:48.000 --> 06:51.000
Even càr, dh’ fheumadh airgead a bhith agad,

06:51.000 --> 06:54.000
a foreigin currency agad son an càr a cheannach.

06:54.000 --> 06:57.000
Dh’fhaodadh millean dolar a bhith agad an New Zealand,

06:57.000 --> 06:59.000
cha cheannaicheadh sin càr dhut.

06:59.000 --> 07:01.000
Dh’fheumadh tu foreign money son, sin mar a bha iad a’…

07:01.000 --> 07:03.000
that’s, sin agad na bha iad a’ dèanamh.

07:03.000 --> 07:05.000
Bha iad mar gun robh na Ruiseanaich.

07:05.000 --> 07:08.000
So, Calum of course, fhuair mi greim air [XX]

07:08.000 --> 07:11.000
a bha seo, transistor radios.

07:11.000 --> 07:14.000
So bhithinn gan ceannach ann an Samoa, ann am Fiji,

07:14.000 --> 07:17.000
agus gan toirt a New Zealand air a’ bhàta.

07:17.000 --> 07:22.000
An uairsin, fear dhen a’ chriutha, thàinig e dìreach ri idea:

07:22.000 --> 07:25.000
gum faigheadh e barailte mòr far am biodh an ola, toll a chur sa…

07:25.000 --> 07:30.000
am bonn a thoirt às, a’ toirt an ola às air fad,

07:30.000 --> 07:33.000
agus ga pàcadh suas ri transistor radios,

07:33.000 --> 07:36.000
’s gan cuir san deic còmhla ri an… còmhla ris an ola!

07:36.000 --> 07:39.000
So, “that’s ok.” Thachair sin, a Dhia,

07:39.000 --> 07:42.000
son dà bhliadhna sin agad a’ [challing/?] a bh’ agam,

07:42.000 --> 07:44.000
a’ reic na rudan a bha seo, a dhol dhan a’ bhàgh,

07:44.000 --> 07:46.000
a thilleadh a-rithist, bhiodh dà bhaga mhòr agam.

07:46.000 --> 07:50.000
[...], sìos dhan a– dha na camps, fhios agad,

07:50.000 --> 07:52.000
construction camps shuas.

07:52.000 --> 07:55.000
Bhiodh iad sa phub, dà uair an uaireadair reicinn an whole lot.

07:55.000 --> 07:59.000
Poidhle mòr de dh’airgead agam agus… [XX].

07:59.000 --> 08:02.000
Ach an latha a bha seo, bha mi a’ smaoineachadh gun robh mi

08:02.000 --> 08:05.000
am Brisbane na an àiteigin, chan eil fhios ’am càit’ robh mi ga reic,

08:05.000 --> 08:07.000
agus bha mi ag èisteachd ri tè dhiubh.

08:07.000 --> 08:10.000
Nach an diabhal nam arrestadh?

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
Fhuair iad a-mach gun robh am barailte ann a shiud,

08:12.000 --> 08:14.000
agus fhuair na customs e, oh my God.

08:14.000 --> 08:18.000
Cha do thill mise dad! But, nuair a thachair sin, 

08:18.000 --> 08:21.000
an Chinaman, a laochain, a bhiodh–

08:21.000 --> 08:23.000
a bhiodh a’ supplieadh na transistor radios, 

08:23.000 --> 08:25.000
thug e dhomhsa baga beag, laghach, mar a…

08:25.000 --> 08:28.000
 mar a bh’ agam nuair a thàinig mi seo.

08:28.000 --> 08:34.000
Tartan, làn… tartan air, agus baga snog a bh’ ann.

08:34.000 --> 08:39.000
So bha sin agamsa. Niste, nuair a dh’fhàg mi,

08:39.000 --> 08:42.000
nuair a dh’aoin mi am bàta, dh’fhàg mi New Zealand.

08:42.000 --> 08:45.000
Thug e dhomhsa e son prèasant so, nuair a thachair…

08:45.000 --> 08:49.000
fhuair iad burst, fhuair iad a-mach gun robh an transistor sa…

08:49.000 --> 08:52.000
san tanca far an robh an ola, that was the end of that business.

08:52.000 --> 08:56.000
So, cha robh, a laochain, ach dh’aoin mi Starboard a-rithist.

08:56.000 --> 09:00.000
So leum mi ann am Panama, an uairsin thill mi air bòrd air.

09:00.000 --> 09:04.000
An uairsin, leum mi a-rithist dhi nuair a chaidh i gu Boston.

09:04.000 --> 09:06.000
Uill, nuair a land i am Boston, a-rithist, 

09:06.000 --> 09:08.000
tàilleabh gum bruidhninn Gàidhlig… 

09:09.000 --> 09:11.000
mo chousin a thàinig còmhla rium air muir,

09:11.000 --> 09:14.000
chaidh mi fhìn ’s e fhèin a-mach còmhla agus m’ uncail,

09:14.000 --> 09:21.000
Ruairidh a’ Phosta. Cousin, no actually, first cousin dhasan,

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
bha i na, tè bha air toiseach – gille-toisich –

09:23.000 --> 09:27.000
aig am Painter’s Union of America. 

09:27.000 --> 09:29.000
So chaidh sinn suas dhan an Union Hall. 

09:29.000 --> 09:33.000
“Oh, not a problem, MacNeil.” Job – peantadh?

09:33.000 --> 09:35.000
“Oh, peantadh, a laochain, all my life!”

09:35.000 --> 09:41.000
Fhuair mi job, bha sin 19… oh I bet you, ’68 or something. 

09:41.000 --> 09:48.000
Anyway, five dollars and twenty-five cents an hour. A fortune!

09:48.000 --> 09:50.000
Iosa, bha dùil ’am gun do dh’eug mi 

09:50.000 --> 09:54.000
’s gun deach mi a Fhlathanas leis an airgead a bha sin, so wow!

09:54.000 --> 09:57.000
That was it. A’ peantadh am Boston Bridge, a h-uile sgath. 

09:57.000 --> 09:59.000
An aon rud, agus bha car de dh’eagal orm ach, 

09:59.000 --> 10:01.000
bruidhinn air eagal, fhios agad nuair a chì thu 

10:01.000 --> 10:03.000
passenger boats fon drochaid?

10:03.000 --> 10:05.000
Fhios agad, an t-einnsean aige a’ dol ‘poof, poof’!

10:05.000 --> 10:08.000
A Mhuire, an drochaid, fhios agad,

10:08.000 --> 10:10.000
cha mhòr nach eil thu air caitheamh far na drochaid 

10:10.000 --> 10:13.000
leis an noise a tha an t-einnsean a’ dèanamh, my God.

10:13.000 --> 10:15.000
Anyway, bha mi sin, so… Ach, cha robh fhios ’am,

10:15.000 --> 10:18.000
an-dràsta ’s a-rithist, bhiodh iad a’ raideadh na jobs a bha seo.

10:18.000 --> 10:21.000
So fhuair iad a-mach air dòigh air choireigin

10:21.000 --> 10:23.000
gun robh mise ann a shiud, mi fhìn ’s a dhà neo trì eile,

10:23.000 --> 10:25.000
cha b’ aithne dhomhsa an fheadhainn eile idir.

10:25.000 --> 10:28.000
Thàinig na poileasman. Uill am boss, 

10:29.000 --> 10:32.000
am fear a bha ann an charge, ruig e ormsa:

10:32.000 --> 10:34.000
“Right,” ars e, “thalla air falach.” 

10:34.000 --> 10:38.000
Agus fhuair iad na, fhios agad, na twenty-five cigarette packet,

10:38.000 --> 10:41.000
fhios agad, na cigarette packages, the twenty-five.

10:41.000 --> 10:46.000
Bha loose plastic, bha rudeigin air a’ chùl aca.

10:46.000 --> 10:50.000
Thug e a-mach e agus sgrìobh e air: ‘Jim’, neo ‘John’,

10:50.000 --> 10:51.000
chan eil cuimhn’ am dè, Jim or something,

10:51.000 --> 10:54.000
‘this is a good man, give him a job’.

10:54.000 --> 10:57.000
Agus thug e dhomh an address airson a dhol gu Cape Cod. 

10:57.000 --> 10:59.000
Ars esan: “Head off to Cape Cod, they’ll never find you there.”

11:00.000 --> 11:03.000
Well, of course, nuair a fhuair mi an t-airgead,

11:03.000 --> 11:05.000
cha do ruig e orm ach tha cuimhn’ am, bha peant agam air a’…

11:05.000 --> 11:09.000
thuit spots de pheant air a’… air an lèine agam 

11:09.000 --> 11:12.000
nuair a chaidh mi a dh’iarraidh an t-airgead an làrna-mhàireach.

11:12.000 --> 11:14.000
So an uairsin dh’fhalbh mi is bha mi 

11:14.000 --> 11:16.000
sa bhus station a’ dol gu Cape Cod.

11:16.000 --> 11:18.000
Agus bha am baga agam, an tartan bag ann a shiud 

11:18.000 --> 11:21.000
’s mo chasan, cigar mòr agam, ‘whew’ a bhalaich,

